    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d685">

                <pb facs="1047" n="1033" xml:id="pg1033"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Japan)/10–748</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Assistant Secretary of State for
                        Occupied Areas</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Saltzman</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the United States Representative on the Far Eastern
                        Commission</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">McCoy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-10-07">October 7, 1948</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Subject: Instructions on Compromise Language for paragraph 1 C
                    of FEC 298/8.</p>
                <p>This will confirm the oral authorization given to Mr. Barnett<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d685-f1"/> to accept the compromise language for this paragraph
                    suggested by the United Kingdom as follows, or closely comparable language to
                    the same effect: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The specific travel authorized herein should be restricted to that
                            deemed essential to meet Japan’s peaceful needs as defined by the FEC
                            and the number of Japanese commercial representatives permitted to
                            travel abroad should be similarly restricted.”<anchor n="2"
                                xml:id="d685-f2"/>
                        </p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles</hi> E. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Saltzman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d685-f1" n="1" xml:id="d685-f1-content">
                <p>Robert W. Barnett, member of the U.S. delegation to the Far Eastern
                    Commission.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d685-f2" n="2" xml:id="d685-f2-content">
                <p>For text as passed by the FEC on October 21, see <hi rendition="#italic">The Far
                        Eastern Commission</hi>, 2d report, p. 36.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
